      "id": "0d13e8f6f278-q19",
      "number": 19,
      "question": "Class has 70 students. Boys = girls. Sakshi is 19th from top, 10 girls ahead. How many boys are behind her?",
      "questionHtml": "<!-- x-tinymce/html -->Class has 70 students. Boys = girls. Sakshi is 19th from top, 10 girls ahead. How many boys are behind her?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "20",
          "html": "20"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "27",
          "html": "27"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "23",
          "html": "23"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "21",
          "html": "21"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p>The logic followed here is:</p>\n\n<p>Total number of students in the class = 70.</p>\n\n<p>Since the number of Boys = the number of Girls, there are 35 Boys and 35 Girls.</p>\n\n<p>Sakshi is 19th from the top, which means there are 18 students ahead of her.</p>\n\n<p>Out of the 18 students ahead of her, 10 are girls.</p>\n\n<p>The number of boys ahead of her = 18 (total students ahead) - 10 (girls ahead) = 8 boys.</p>\n\n<p>Total number of boys in the class = 35.</p>\n\n<p>Number of boys behind Sakshi = Total Boys - Boys ahead of Sakshi</p>\n\n<p>= 35 - 8 = 27 boys.</p>\n\n<p>Hence, the correct answer is &quot;<strong>Option 2</strong>&quot;.</p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
